I served in the United States Marine  Corps for four and a half years I found  Hillsdale at the end of my last  deployment applied and came here  basically three weeks later  Hillsdale stood out from the other  colleges that I was looking at and that  it emphasized teaching you how to learn  not what to think and so I felt like I  could take that and kind of become a  learner for the rest of my life rather  than just learning for four years once I  decided to come to Hillsdale the big  flashing question was what about  financial aid I was just so impressed  with how eager they were to help me get  here private donors had stepped in and  ended up providing basically a full ride  for me the full four years here at  Hillsdale and it's amazing to see that  because they understand how valuable  this is I think for most of the people  coming from the military they already  have this deep sense of love and respect  for our country but there's a lot of  room for understanding what that country  is and the things that really that  established it and have preserved it the  liberal arts and the education here will  not only give you that but so much more  this foundation not just for government  and how we live in society together but  in your own life an understanding of  what it means to be human and how to  live the best life you'll be able to  apply that and take that to whatever  career path or wherever it is you go or  whatever that you want to do that's  going to inform every aspect of your  life
 

